# Ignore rules that apply to PRETTIER ONLY.
#
# oxfmt reads `.prettierignore` as well as `.gitignore`
# (https://oxc.rs/docs/guide/usage/formatter/ignore-files.html), so `.prettierignore`
# is now a SHARED file: anything listed there is invisible to both formatters. A rule
# meant for one tool has to live somewhere the other tool does not read. This is that
# file — Prettier gets it via `--ignore-path`, oxfmt never sees it.
#
# Everything below belongs to oxfmt. Listing it here is what stops `yarn format:prettier`
# from walking in and reformatting the 98% of the workspace oxfmt owns.
*.ts
*.tsx
*.mts
*.cts
*.js
*.jsx
*.mjs
*.cjs
*.json
*.jsonc
*.json5
*.css
*.scss
*.less
*.md
*.markdown
*.yml
*.yaml

# Angular component templates go to oxfmt too — the `.component.html` suffix is how
# oxfmt knows to use its Angular parser. Prettier must not touch these either.
*.component.html
